// Book · O Research: every step a side may learn, one entry a code, in Mid's table order (a line's steps come in this order). An entry's value = {at, line, age, cost, time, fx: [{s, k, p|a|min}], need, when, w}: at the shell where it is learned; line its line there; s the number it changes (spd, hp, atk, rng, rof, rate, cost, time, or a key its consumer reads), k the keys it reaches (a shell's code, any of its letters' heads, a tick, a soldier's class, or '*'), p a share that adds (+0.10 is 10%; Mid's ×m is p = m − 1), a a flat add (Mid's pixels ÷ D12 for a reach), min the lowest kept; need the steps it waits on besides the one before it, by key; tier (when a step has one) the look it raises a level (Mid's btier; the tower's steps come with M21); rank (when a step has one) the soldier kind it raises a level and renames (Mid's tier: its shares and adds sit in fx like any other, added, and its counter in vs for the blow); kit a step a soldier's figure wears (the armour: leather, chain, plate); when its date; w its weight in history, 1 to 10. Its effects are applied by one law (QCA). Edit here only.
